  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The heading printed over an Epistle of St Paul. LÉCTIO is the nominative of a heading: no verb is expressed or understood. EPÍSTOLÆ is the genitive of the letter the reading is taken from; BEÁTI agrees with PAULI, and APÓSTOLI stands in apposition to it. AD with the accusative names those to whom the letter was written. EPHÉSIOS is an adjective used as a noun.",
    "source": {
      "method": "The Latin follows the Benziger Brothers 1962 editio iuxta typicam, which prints this heading over the Epistle on printed p. 407 (IA leaf n488 / PDF p. 489) and over the 8 further readings named in the witness header; it is compared with the heading line of the pinned Divinum Officium file that the reading's own digital witness binds. Source review remains pending.",
